# Canonical verification tests

`Test` contains the entry points for application-independent and IYDT
verification suites. These are calculation checks, not unit tests managed by an
R package framework.

## Supplied suites

| Suite | Runner | Scope |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `global` | `tests.r` | covariance Jacobians, FME/RAM/NUTS/SMC backends, and unbounded/bounded/transformed observed-information assertions |
| `IYDT/Seismic` | `IYDT/Seismic/tests.r` | seismic forward-model and Jacobian cases |
| `IYDT/Acoustic` | `IYDT/Acoustic/tests.r` | acoustic forward-model and Jacobian cases |
| `IYDT/Optical` | `IYDT/Optical/tests.r` | optical forward-model and Jacobian cases |
| `IYDT/Crater` | `IYDT/Crater/tests.r` | crater forward-model and Jacobian cases |
| `IYDT/Data` | `IYDT/Data/tests.r` | production data contracts and model integration |
| `IYDT/Transform` | `IYDT/Transform/tests.r` | event transforms and analytical derivatives |
| `IYDT/Prior` | `IYDT/Prior/tests.r` | application prior densities and gradients |
| `IYDT/Checkpoint` | `IYDT/Checkpoint/tests.r` | calibration checkpoint preservation and event reuse |
| `IYDT/Contract` | `IYDT/Contract/tests.r` | rejection of malformed, incomplete, and non-finite model inputs |
| `IYDT/Summary` | `IYDT/Summary/tests.r` | calibration and event summary-output structure |
| `IYDT/Runfile` | `IYDT/Runfile/tests.r` | reduced real calibration/event runfile execution and pristine-checkpoint preservation |
| `IYDT/Bayes` | `IYDT/Bayes/tests.r` | bounded fixed-seed Bayesian calibration/event execution plus likelihood, posterior, and EIV derivative checks |
| `IYDT/Bayes-Backends` | `IYDT/Bayes-Backends/tests.r` | bounded real-application RAM and NUTS calibration/event execution |
| `IYDT/MultiPhenomenology` | `IYDT/MultiPhenomenology/tests.r` | optical/crater integration using staged single-phenomenology optimization inputs |
| `IYDT/Parallel` | `IYDT/Parallel/tests.r` | one-worker/two-worker deterministic calibration/event equivalence |
| `IYDT/Prediction` | `IYDT/Prediction/tests.r` | direct forward-model agreement plus observation and covariance identities |
| `IYDT/Profile` | `IYDT/Profile/tests.r` | reduced profile-likelihood optimization and plot generation |
| `IYDT/Imputation` | `IYDT/Imputation/tests.r` | two-imputation RAM/SMC inference, pooled samples, diagnostics, and checkpoint preservation |

The global runner sources `Code/test_cov.r`, `Code/test_fme.r`,
`Code/test_samplers.r`, `Code/test_smc.r`, and `Code/test_information.r`.
The sampler checks use
a fixed-seed correlated Gaussian target to assert posterior moments,
reproducibility, acceptance diagnostics, and identical callback/fused NUTS
results. The SMC checks add exact sequential reproducibility, one-worker versus
two-worker statistical agreement, adaptive and warning-only range controls,
particle-pool sampling with and without replacement, ESS/weight arithmetic,
mixed and total non-finite-density handling, range validation, and an
all-zero-mass failure assertion. The
information checks compare calibration and event covariance
blocks with the inverse of a numerical Hessian and exercise the one-sided,
two-sided, and application-transform chain-rule branches. The IYDT
runners source canonical application code from `Applications/Code/IYDT-gsrp`
and fixtures from `Applications/Test/IYDT`. IYDT Jacobian checks are
assertions: a dimension, finite-value, or tolerance mismatch produces a
nonzero exit status.

## Recommended Docker workflow

From `../Test-Docker`:

```text
Rscript testmpem.R doctor
Rscript testmpem.R build
Rscript testmpem.R list
Rscript testmpem.R run global
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Seismic
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Acoustic
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Optical
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Crater
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Data
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Transform
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Prior
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Checkpoint
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Contract
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Summary
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Runfile
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Bayes
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Bayes-Backends
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/MultiPhenomenology
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Parallel
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Prediction
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Profile
Rscript testmpem.R run IYDT/Imputation
```

Each command creates an isolated snapshot and prints a job name and results
directory. Use `status`, `logs -f`, `wait`, and `clean` as documented in
`../Test-Docker/README`. Docker is preferred because it pins R packages and
prevents test output from modifying canonical source directories.

## Native workflow

Install at least `Matrix`, `numDeriv`, `FME`, `adaptMCMC`, `Rcpp`, and
`RcppEigen`. From `Test`, create the shared code link:

```text
ln -s ../Code Code
```

Run the global suite from this directory:

```text
R CMD BATCH tests.r tests.out &
```

For IYDT suites, first create the links described in `IYDT/README`, then run
from the chosen suite directory, for example:

```text
cd IYDT/Seismic
R CMD BATCH tests.r tests.out &
```

The trailing `&` returns the shell prompt while the suite runs. Follow progress
with `tail -f tests.out` and inspect the final transcript and process status.

Each runner saves `.RData` and prints named test sections to `tests.out`.
Inspect the complete transcript and the process exit status; do not infer
success merely from the presence of output files.

Test workspaces are disposable. For real benchmarking or calibration runs,
preserve a pristine `.RData` checkpoint before any event analysis and use a
copy for each event so event results cannot overwrite the reusable baseline.

## Adding tests

Application-independent checks belong in `../Code` and are sourced by
`tests.r`. Application-specific fixtures belong under `../Applications/Test`;
their suite runner belongs under `Test/GROUP/SUITE/tests.r`.

Register a new group in `../Test-Docker/test-groups.tsv`. A new suite beneath
an existing group is discovered automatically. Run `testmpem.R doctor`, list
the suites, and execute every affected suite after a change.
